#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:12
msgid "Fluid Mechanics Derivations"
msgstr "Derivaciones en mecánica de fluidos"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:19
msgid "Minor Loss Equation"
msgstr "Ecuación de pérdida menor"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:21
msgid ""
"This section contains the derivation of the minor loss equation using the "
"following figure as a reference. The derivation begins with a slightly "
"simplified energy equation across the control volume shown. Our energy "
"equation begins with :math:`h_P` and :math:`h_T` having been eliminated."
msgstr ""
"Esta sección contiene la derivación de la ecuación de pérdida menor usando "
"la siguiente figura como referencia. La derivación comienza con una ecuación"
" de energía ligeramente simplificada a lo largo del volumen de control "
"mostrado. Nuestra ecuación de energía comienza con :math:`h_P` y :math:`h_T`"
" habiendo sido eliminados."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:31
msgid "Example of flow expansion resulting in a minor loss"
msgstr "Ejemplo de expansión del flujo que resulta en una pérdida menor"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:31
msgid "This is the system we will use to derive the minor loss equation."
msgstr "Este es el sistema que usaremos para derivar la ecuación de la pérdida menor."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:33
msgid ""
"\\frac{p_{in}}{\\rho g} + {z_{in}} + \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2}{2g} = "
"\\frac{p_{out}}{\\rho g} + z_{out} + \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2}{2g} + h_L"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:37
msgid ""
"Since the elevations at the center of the :math:`in` and :math:`out` control"
" surfaces are the same, we can eliminate :math:`z_{in}` and :math:`z_{out}`."
" As we are considering such a small length of pipe, we will neglect the "
"major loss component of head loss. Thus, :math:`h_L = h_e + \\cancel{h_f}`. "
"The following three equations are all the same, simply rearranged to solve "
"for :math:`h_e`."
msgstr ""
"Dado que las elevaciones en el centro de la :math:`in` y :math:`out` "
"superficies de control son las mismas, podemos eliminar :math:`z_{in}` y "
":math:`z_{out}`. Como consideramos un tramo de tubería tan pequeño, "
"descuidaremos el componente principal de pérdida de pérdida de carga. Así, "
":math:`h_L = h_e + \\cancel{h_f}`. Las siguientes tres ecuaciones son todas "
"iguales, simplemente reordenadas para resolver :math:`h_e`."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:39
msgid ""
"\\frac{p_{in}}{\\rho g} + \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2}{2g} = \\frac{p_{out}}{\\rho"
" g} + \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2}{2g} + h_e"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:43
msgid ""
"\\frac{p_{in} - p_{out}}{\\rho g} = \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - \\bar "
"v_{in}^2}{2g} + h_e"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:47
msgid ""
"  h_e = \\frac{p_{in} - p_{out}}{\\rho g} + \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2 - \\bar "
"v_{out}^2}{2g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:52
msgid ""
"This last equation has :math:`h_e` as a function of four variables "
":math:`(p_{in}, \\, p_{out}, \\, v_{in}`, and :math:`v_{out})`; we would "
"like it to be a function of only one. Thus, we will invoke conservation of "
"momentum in the horizontal direction across our control volume to remove "
"variables. The difference in momentum from the :math:`in` point to the "
":math:`out` point is driven by the pressure difference between each end of "
"the control volume. We will be considering the pressure at the centroid of "
"our control surfaces, and we will neglect shear along the pipe walls. After "
"these assumptions, our momentum equation becomes the following:"
msgstr ""
"Esta última ecuación :math:`h_e` como función de cuatro variables "
":math:`(p_{in}, \\, p_{out}, \\, v_{in}`, y :math:`v_{out})`; nos gustaría "
"que fuera función de una sola. Así, invocaremos la conservación del momento "
"en la dirección horizontal a través de nuestro volumen de control para "
"eliminar variables. La diferencia de momento desde el punto de :math:`in` "
"hasta el punto :math:`out` está determinada por la diferencia de presión "
"entre cada extremo del volumen de control. Consideraremos la presión en el "
"centroide de nuestras superficies de control y descuidaremos el corte a lo "
"largo de las paredes de la tubería. Tras estas suposiciones, nuestra "
"ecuación de momento pasa a ser la siguiente:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:54
msgid "M_{in, \\, x} + M_{out, \\, x} = F_{p_{in, \\, x}} + F_{p_{out, \\, x}}"
msgstr "M_{in, \\, x} + M_{out, \\, x} = F_{p_{in, \\, x}} + F_{p_{out, \\, x}}"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:58
msgid "Such that:"
msgstr "Tal que:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:59
msgid ""
":math:`M_{x}` = momentum flowing through the control volume in the "
"x-direction"
msgstr ""
":math:`M_{x}` = momento que fluye a través del volumen de control en la "
"dirección x"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:60
msgid ""
":math:`F_{p_x}` = force due to pressure acting on the boundaries of the "
"control volume in the x-direction"
msgstr ""
":math:`F_{p_x}` = fuerza debida a la presión que actúa sobre los límites del"
" volumen de control en la dirección x"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:62
msgid ""
"Recall that momentum is mass times velocity for solids, :math:`m v`, with "
"units of :math:`\\frac{[M][L]}{[T]}`. Since we consider water flowing "
"through a pipe, there is not one singular mass or one singular velocity. "
"Instead, there is a mass flow rate, or a mass per time indicated by "
":math:`\\dot m = \\rho Q`, which has units of :math:`\\frac{[M]}{[T]}`. "
"Therefore, the momentum for a fluid is :math:`\\rho Q \\bar v`. Applying the"
" continuity Equation :math:`Q = \\bar v A`, we get to the following equation"
" for the momentum of a fluid flowing through a pipe which we will use in "
"this derivation, :math:`M = \\rho \\bar v^2 A`. The pressure force is simply"
" the pressure at the centroid of the flow multiplied by the area the "
"pressure is acting upon, :math:`p A`."
msgstr ""
"Recordemos que el momento es masa por velocidad para sólidos, :math:`m v`, "
"con unidades de :math:`\\frac{[M][L]}{[T]}`. Dado que consideramos el agua "
"fluyendo a través de una tubería, no hay una masa única ni una velocidad "
"singular. En su lugar, existe una masa caudal, o una masa por tiempo "
"indicada por :math:`\\dot m = \\rho Q`, que tiene unidades de "
":math:`\\frac{[M]}{[T]}`. Por lo tanto, el momento para un fluido es "
":math:`\\rho Q \\bar v`. Aplicando la ecuación de continuidad :math:`Q = "
"\\bar v A`, obtenemos la siguiente ecuación para el momento de un fluido que"
" fluye a través de una tubería que usaremos en esta deducción, :math:`M = "
"\\rho \\bar v^2 A`. La fuerza de presión es simplemente la presión en el "
"centroide del flujo multiplicada por el área sobre la que actúa la presión, "
":math:`p A`."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:64
msgid ""
"To ensure correct sign convention, we will make each side of the equation "
"negative for reasons discussed shortly. Since :math:`\\bar v_{in} > \\bar "
"v_{out}`, the left hand side will be :math:`M_{out} - M_{in}` in order to be"
" negative. The reduction in velocity from :math:`in` to :math:`out` causes "
"an increase in pressure, therefore :math:`p_{in} - p_{out}` is negative. "
"With these substitutions, the conservation of momentum equation becomes as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""
"Para asegurar la convención correcta de signos, haremos que cada lado de la "
"ecuación sea negativo por razones que se explicarán más adelante. Dado que "
":math:`\\bar v_{in} > \\bar v_{out}`, el lado izquierdo se :math:`M_{out} - "
"M_{in}` para que sea negativo. La reducción de velocidad de :math:`in` a "
":math:`out` provoca un aumento de presión, por lo tanto :math:`p_{in} - "
"p_{out}` es negativo. Con estas sustituciones, la ecuación de conservación "
"del momento es la siguiente:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:66
msgid "M_{out} - M_{in} = p_{in} - p_{out}"
msgstr "M_{out} - M_{in} = p_{in} - p_{out}"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:70
msgid ""
"\\rho \\bar v_{out}^2 A_{out} - \\rho \\bar v_{in}^2 A_{in} = p_{in} A_{out}"
" - p_{out} A_{out}"
msgstr ""
"\\rho \\bar v_{out}^2 A_{out} - \\rho \\bar v_{in}^2 A_{in} = p_{in} A_{out}"
" - p_{out} A_{out}"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:74
msgid ""
"Note that the area term attached to :math:`p_{in}` is actually "
":math:`A_{out}` instead of :math:`A_{in}`, as one might think. This is "
"because :math:`A_{out} = A_{in}`. We chose our control volume to start a few"
" millimeters into the larger pipe, which means that the cross-sectional area"
" does not change over the course of the control volume."
msgstr ""
"Nótese que el término de área asociado a :math:`p_{in}` es en realidad "
":math:`A_{out}` en lugar de :math:`A_{in}`, como se podría pensar. Esto se "
"debe a :math:`A_{out} = A_{in}`. Elegimos nuestro volumen de control para "
"empezar unos milímetros dentro de la tubería más grande, lo que significa "
"que el área de la sección transversal no cambia a lo largo del volumen de "
"control."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:76
msgid ""
"Dividing both sides of the equation by :math:`A_{out} \\rho g`, we obtain "
"the following equation, which contains the very same pressure term as our "
"adjusted energy equation above, Equation :eq:`minor_loss_energy_eq`. This is"
" why we chose a negative sign convention."
msgstr ""
"Dividiendo ambos lados de la ecuación por :math:`A_{out} \\rho g`, obtenemos"
" la siguiente ecuación, que contiene el mismo término de presión que nuestra"
" ecuación de energía ajustada anterior, Ecuación :eq:`minor_loss_energy_eq`."
" Por eso elegimos una convención de signo negativo."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:78
msgid ""
"\\frac{p_{in} - p_{out}}{\\rho g} = \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - \\bar v_{in}^2 "
"\\frac{A_{in}}{A_{out}}}{g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:82
msgid "Now, we combine the momentum, continuity, and adjusted energy equations:"
msgstr "Ahora, combinamos las ecuaciones de momento, continuidad y energía ajustada:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:84
msgid ""
"{\\rm{Energy \\, equation:}} \\,\\,\\,  h_e = \\frac{p_{in} - p_{out}}{\\rho"
" g} + \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2 - \\bar v_{out}^2}{2g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:88
msgid ""
"{\\rm{Momentum \\, equation:}} \\,\\,\\, \\frac{p_{in} - p_{out}}{\\rho g} ="
" \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - \\bar v_{in}^2 \\frac{A_{in}}{A_{out}}}{g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:92
msgid ""
"{\\rm{Continuity \\, equation:}} \\,\\,\\, \\frac{A_{in}}{A_{out}} = "
"\\frac{\\bar v_{out}}{\\bar v_{in}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:96
msgid ""
"To obtain an equation for minor losses with just two variables, :math:`\\bar"
" v_{in}` and :math:`\\bar v_{out}`."
msgstr ""
"Para obtener una ecuación para pérdidas menores con solo dos variables, "
":math:`\\bar v_{in}` y :math:`\\bar v_{out}`."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:98
msgid ""
"h_e = \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - \\bar v_{in}^2\\frac{\\bar v_{out}}{\\bar "
"v_{in}}}{g} + \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2 - \\bar v_{out}^2}{2g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:102
msgid ""
"Now we will combine the two terms. The numerator and denominator of the "
"first term, :math:`\\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - \\bar v_{in}^2\\frac{\\bar "
"v_{out}}{\\bar v_{in}}}{g}` will be multiplied by :math:`2` to become "
":math:`\\frac{2 \\bar v_{out}^2 - 2 \\bar v_{in}^2\\frac{\\bar "
"v_{out}}{\\bar v_{in}}}{2 g}`. The equation then looks like:"
msgstr ""
"Ahora vamos a combinar los dos términos. El numerador y denominador del "
"primer término, :math:`\\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - \\bar v_{in}^2\\frac{\\bar "
"v_{out}}{\\bar v_{in}}}{g}` se multiplicarán por :math:`2` para obtener "
":math:`\\frac{2 \\bar v_{out}^2 - 2 \\bar v_{in}^2\\frac{\\bar "
"v_{out}}{\\bar v_{in}}}{2 g}`. La ecuación entonces se presenta así:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:104
msgid ""
"h_e = \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2 - 2 \\bar v_{in} \\bar v_{out} + \\bar "
"v_{in}^2}{2g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:112
msgid "Final Forms of the Minor Loss Equation"
msgstr "Formas finales de la ecuación de la pérdida menor"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:114
msgid ""
"Factoring the numerator yields to the first ‘final’ form of the minor loss "
"equation:"
msgstr ""
"Al factorizar el numerador, se obtiene la primera forma 'final' de la "
"ecuación de pérdida menor:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:116
msgid ""
"{\\rm{ \\mathbf{First \\, form:} }} \\quad h_e = \\frac{\\left( \\bar v_{in}"
"  - \\bar v_{out} \\right)^2}{2g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:120
msgid ""
"From here, the two other forms of the minor loss equation can be derived by "
"solving for either :math:`\\bar v_{in}` or :math:`\\bar v_{out}` using the "
"ubiquitous continuity Equation :math:`\\bar v_{in} A_{in} = \\bar v_{out} "
"A_{out}`:"
msgstr ""
"A partir de aquí, las otras dos formas de la ecuación de pérdida menor "
"pueden derivarse resolviendo para :math:`\\bar v_{in}` o :math:`\\bar "
"v_{out}` usando la ubicua ecuación de continuidad :math:`\\bar v_{in} A_{in}"
" = \\bar v_{out} A_{out}`:"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:122
msgid ""
"{\\rm{ \\mathbf{Second \\, form:} }} \\quad h_e = \\left( 1 - "
"\\frac{A_{in}}{A_{out}} \\right)^2 \\, \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2}{2g} \\, \\, = "
"\\, \\, K_e^{'} \\frac{\\bar v_{in}^2}{2g}, \\quad {\\rm where} \\quad "
"K_e^{'} = \\left( 1 - \\frac{A_{in}}{A_{out}} \\right)^2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:126
msgid ""
"   {\\rm{ \\mathbf{Third \\, form:} }} \\quad h_e = \\left( "
"\\frac{A_{out}}{A_{in}} -1 \\right)^2 \\, \\frac{\\bar  v_{out}^2}{2g} \\, "
"\\, = \\, \\, K_e \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2}{2g}, \\quad {\\rm where} \\quad "
"K_e = \\left( \\frac{A_{out}}{A_{in}} - 1 \\right)^2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:133
msgid ""
"You will often see :math:`K_e^{'}` and :math:`K_e` used without the "
":math:`e` subscript, they will appear as :math:`K^{'}` and :math:`K`."
msgstr ""
"A menudo verás :math:`K_e^{'}` y :math:`K_e` usados sin el :math:`e` "
"subíndice, aparecerán como :math:`K^{'}` y :math:`K`."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:135
msgid ""
"Being familiar with these three forms and how they are used will be of great"
" help throughout the class. The third form is the one that is most commonly "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Familiarizarse con estas tres formas y cómo se utilizan será de gran ayuda "
"durante toda la clase. La tercera forma es la que se usa con más frecuencia."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:137
msgid ""
"We can convert the minor loss coefficient, :math:`K_e`, into a flow "
"contraction using the minor loss equation (see Equation "
":eq:`minor_loss_equation`)"
msgstr ""
"Podemos convertir el coeficiente de pérdida menor, :math:`K_e`, en una "
"contracción de flujo usando la ecuación de pérdida menor (véase la ecuación "
":eq:`minor_loss_equation`)"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:139
msgid " K_e = \\left(\\frac{1}{\\Pi_{vc}}  - 1 \\right)^2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:144
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` is the ratio of the contracted area to the full "
"expanded flow area."
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` es la relación entre el área contraída y el área de "
"flujo expandida completa."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:146
msgid "\\Pi_{vc} = \\frac{A_{in}}{A_{out}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:151
msgid ""
"Given that :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` is the ratio of the contracted area to the full"
" expanded flow area we obtain the relationship between the contracted "
"diameter, :math:`D_{vc}`, and the expanded diameter, :math:`D_{pipe}`."
msgstr ""
"Dado que :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` es la relación entre el área contraída y el área "
"de flujo expandida completa, obtenemos la relación entre el diámetro "
"contraído, :math:`D_{vc}`, y el diámetro expandido, :math:`D_{pipe}`."

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:153
msgid "D_{pipe} = \\frac{D_{vc}}{\\sqrt{\\Pi_{vc}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:158
msgid "Solving Equation :eq:`minor_K_of_pi_vc` for :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` we obtain"
msgstr "Resolver la ecuación :eq:`minor_K_of_pi_vc` para :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` obtenemos"

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:160
msgid "\\Pi_{vc} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{K_e} + 1}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Fluids_and_Hydraulics/Fluid_Mechanics_Derivations.rst:165
msgid ""
"The extent of a flow contraction, :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` can be estimated from "
"the measured minor loss coefficient."
msgstr ""
"La extensión de una contracción de flujo, :math:`\\Pi_{vc}` puede estimarse "
"a partir del coeficiente de pérdida menor medido."

